**/__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# napi-rs native addon build output
/crates/threers-node/*.node
/crates/threers-node/node_modules/
/crates/threers-node/*.tgz
/crates/threers-node/npm/**/*.node
# Accidental create-npm-dir output keyed by rustc triple
/crates/threers-node/aarch64-*/
/crates/threers-node/x86_64-*/

# NASA Earth imagery and everything derived from it -- 6.2 GB, none of it ours.
#
# It was never committed, which is why .git is 13 MB and not 6 GB, but nothing
# said so and one `git add -A` would have ended that. The sources are public and
# fetchable; the derived maps and tiles are reproducible from them:
#
#   scripts/fetch-earth-textures.sh --help    # what each flag costs to download
#   scripts/fetch-earth-textures.sh            # base set, ~4 MB
#   scripts/fetch-earth-textures.sh --tiles --sky --png   # the lot
#
# or, equivalently, through the example that also verifies what is present:
#
#   cargo run --release --example earth_assets -- check
#   cargo run --release --example earth_assets -- fetch
#
# CREDITS is tracked deliberately: it is the manifest of what everything is and
# where it came from, and it is the one file here worth keeping in history.
# Note the `/*`: ignoring the *directory* would stop git descending into it, and
# the negation below would never get a chance to fire — which is exactly what
# used to happen here, so CREDITS was ignored along with the imagery.
/web/assets/earth/*
!/web/assets/earth/CREDITS

# Probe demo: generated Cornell planes + copied hops/NRC weights
/web/assets/probe/
webdriver.json

# Staged static site (`node web/scripts/stage-site.mjs`).
/site/
# Example and build output that was committed by accident: the path tracer's
# autosave (16 MB, `examples/viewport_path_trace.rs`) and the Python extension
# maturin builds in place (9 MB, rebuilt on every `maturin develop`). Ignoring
# does not untrack them; `git rm --cached` both.
/viewport_path_trace.rtfc
*.rtfc
/crates/threers-py/python/threers/_native*.so
/crates/threers-py/python/threers/_native*.pyd
